<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="59663" href="schedule/2013/spring/INFO/199/59663.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2013" href="schedule/2013.xml">2013</calendarYear><term id="120131" href="schedule/2013/spring.xml">Spring 2013</term><subject id="INFO" href="schedule/2013/spring/INFO.xml">Informatics</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2013/spring/INFO/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>JC </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Diversity by the Numbers</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 11-Mar-13 - 01-May-13.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course is intended to introduce students to the nature, uses, sources and computational analysis of statistical data that can be used and misused to give a perspective on race and ethnicity in the US.  It will also provide an introduction to the social theories and issues that explain the patterns that will be revealed by our analyses.  The class will meet in a computer lab, a seminar room and will require student completion of an on-line module that will teach straightforward techniques in Microsoft Excel and SPSS via online modules.  Meets With SOC 196.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2013-03-11Z</startDate><endDate>2013-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>05:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>M      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G8A</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Chapa" firstName="J">Chapa, J</instructor></instructors></meeting><meeting id="1"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>G48</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages